# Calls `r acl setuser slowlog-test-user +get +set` uncaught at slowlog.tcl:57, so once
# ACL SETUSER correctly refuses (no rule engine to apply it to) the test aborts instead of
# failing an assertion. It asserts SETUSER args are redacted in SLOWLOG, a feature that needs
# a working SETUSER — genuinely out of reach, not merely inconvenient. compat/delta.md item 7.
SLOWLOG - Certain commands are omitted that contain sensitive information
